TITLE:: PianoRollTimeline
SUMMARY:: Beat grid strip for a piano roll, anchored to the top of a scrolling roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollTimeline:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: whose LINK::Classes/View:: sits above the note area inside the same LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: as LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::. Vertical scrolling of the roll updates the strip so it stays aligned with the visible top edge. Horizontal beat lines use the same spacing as the piano roll. If LINK::#-new:: is given a LINK::Classes/Function::, a single left click sets the loop start, a single right click sets the loop end, and a single left click while holding Shift sets the playback head, each via LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: (see that class for snap and validation rules).

NOTE::
Pass a width in pixels that matches the scrollable piano-roll document (for example the roll LINK::Classes/UserView:: width), not the LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: viewport width alone.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollTimeline:: and installs a scroll LINK::Classes/View#-action:: handler on the given roll that keeps the strip vertically aligned with the scroll view's visible origin. Any previous scroll action is invoked first. Strip height is fixed at 20 pixels.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: that contains the piano roll; the timeline is parented here.

ARGUMENT:: width
Width of the strip in pixels; should match the horizontal extent of the roll content (see NOTE).

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: for background and grid line colours.

ARGUMENT:: horizontalScale
Pixels per beat, matching the piano roll's horizontal scale.

ARGUMENT:: loopClickFunc
Optional LINK::Classes/Function:: evaluated as CODE::func.value(beat, buttonNumber, modifiers):: on a single left (0) or right (1) click. Beat is the click x-coordinate divided by horizontalScale. The LINK::Classes/Integer:: modifiers value is the same style as other LINK::Classes/View:: mouse actions (e.g. LINK::Classes/Integer#-isShift:: for Shift). Pass nil to disable click handling.

PRIVATE:: init
